ONE THING THIS RUN EXPOSED THAT IS NOT MINE TO FIX HERE
-------------------------------------------------------
The turn ended `✓ SUCCESS done in 30s` and calc.py was NEVER EDITED:

    files the toolbar saw written : []
    calc.py now:
        def divide(a, b):
            return a / b

The 3B created a contract, read the file three times, called contract_status,
read a symbol, and stopped. No write tool was ever called and the verdict still
said success. That is the mirror image of the 2026-08-21 bug where a real
`replace_symbol` reported failure because nothing had been journalled - and it
is worth its own pass. Logged here, not fixed here (CLAUDE.md §8, one issue at
a time).

Also worth noting from the same trace: `calc.py is unchanged since the last
read; did not resend it` - a read-dedup already exists, which is relevant to
sizing spec fix 06.


WHAT I COULD NOT TEST
---------------------
An end-to-end run on a real Windows TTY. This session has no console, so
`patch_stdout` lifting live output above a live prompt is covered by
prompt_toolkit's own contract rather than by an assertion of mine.

The next closest thing IS tested: `test_the_real_prompt_session_renders_the_
real_toolbar` drives the actual session `_make_prompt_session` builds, with the
actual toolbar callable, over `create_pipe_input()` + `DummyOutput()`, and
asserts prompt_toolkit invoked the toolbar and rendered `rnd 3/24` and `71%`.
A toolbar that raises, or a session built wrong, fails there.


SAYING SO AT STARTUP
--------------------
The first restart onto this build looked EXACTLY like the old one, and the
session log said why:

    07:34:48  session.started
    08:46:14  session.resumed      <- the restart
    (no user message; messages.jsonl does not exist)

Everything here happens DURING a turn. At an idle prompt the screen is
deliberately identical to before, so a fresh REPL is indistinguishable from an
old one until you send a prompt - and "is the new interface actually running?"
had no answer short of starting a turn and watching one.

    Live console on - type while the agent works, `/context` answers without
    costing tokens, `/queue add <task>` runs after this turn.

    Live console off (stdin is not a terminal) - turns render as a plain log.
    Live console off (SHAMSU_LIVE_FEEDBACK=0) - turns render as a plain log.

The reason is recorded, not guessed at, because "the new interface is not
showing up" and "this terminal cannot host it" look identical from outside.


A MEASUREMENT TRAP WORTH RECORDING
----------------------------------
The first full-suite run came back 2 failed / 3619 passed:

    test_routing_matrix.py::test_every_rule_label_has_a_dispatch_branch
    test_simple_chat.py::test_simple_mode_short_circuits_the_router

Both call `inspect.getsource(repl._handle_request)`, and both were handed a
DIFFERENT function's body - `_approval_watcher`. Neither is a regression:
`repl.py` was edited WHILE the suite ran, which shifted every line number under
`linecache`'s cached copy of the file. Re-run against the stable file, both
pass, and the clean run is green.

Do not edit a file mid-suite in this repo. Several tests read source text by
line offset and they will report a failure that does not exist.


