Worth naming:

    test_a_narrow_terminal_keeps_the_queues_and_gives_up_the_file_list
        seven widths, 110 down to 44. Asserts the round budget, the context
        percentage and both queue depths survive every one of them.
    test_a_read_only_command_runs_locally_and_never_reaches_the_model
    test_a_command_is_dispatched_and_never_queued_for_the_model
        asserts the feedback queue is EMPTY afterwards - a command that also
        reached the model would pass a weaker test.
    test_a_state_changing_command_is_deferred_not_run
        `/compact clear` mid-turn would rewrite the history the model is being
        sent on the very next round.
    test_every_whitelisted_command_has_a_handler_behind_it
        walks MIDTURN_COMMANDS and calls each one for real.
    test_the_prompt_stands_down_while_an_approval_is_waiting
        two prompt_toolkit applications cannot share a terminal. This is the
        run_in_executor+stdin trap that used to hang turns on Windows.
    test_the_approval_prompt_takes_the_terminal_synchronously
        the same thing without the polling delay, plus: unregistering really
        unregisters, or a stale observer on a dead console fires on every
        approval for the rest of the session.
    test_a_broken_observer_never_stops_a_human_being_asked
    test_the_two_prompts_share_one_history
        the idle prompt and the mid-turn prompt are two PromptSessions; with a
        history each, something typed while the agent was working could not be
        recalled with Up at the next prompt.
    test_the_turn_still_runs_without_a_live_console
        a pipe, a CI runner, a console with no screen buffer. The fallback is
        not a degraded mode - it is what every turn did before this.
    test_a_read_does_not_count_as_a_file_modified
    test_the_directory_survives_so_two_files_cannot_read_as_one
        `js/config.py` and `css/config.py` are different files.
    test_an_unknown_context_says_so_rather_than_showing_zero
        a meter reading 0% is a claim; an empty window is not an unmeasured one.
    test_a_malformed_event_never_takes_the_prompt_down
        an exception inside a toolbar renderer kills the prompt.
    test_a_queued_task_is_taken_exactly_once
    test_startup_says_WHY_the_live_console_is_off
        "the new interface is not showing up" and "this terminal cannot host
        it" look identical from the outside.
